      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This would be very helpful. You can *mostly* get by with turning particle systems on and off, but this adds a layer of indirection when you want to trigger a burst (a parent emitter has to trigger a sub-emitter). That setup also means that the child emitter's particles go away when the parent's game object is deactivated.\n\nYou *can* unparent the sub-emitter's object, but this causes some weird behaviors – I'm pretty sure you aren't meant to do that.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-02-16T13:02:33.790Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In the same respect as giving us a means to directly trigger audio sources through an animator (which is fantastic btw), it'd be useful to be able to trigger Particle Emission in the same fashion via an animator Behaviour to do things like consistently fire single-shot guns.",
